    "findings": [
      "The RGB control equals or beats learned palettes overall: 13 versus 11 checked pairs, no learned-only checked gain. Both methods restore details that raw low-resolution neural masks erased.",
      "Printed red trees: RGB clustering recovers the coarse paper checker (0.474% fit error); neural-selected colours follow printed ink instead (3.180%). The masks differ by 34.3106%, so this is a material-target failure before fitting.",
      "Shaded red/gold checker: masks differ by 3.90125%, RGB fit error 2.48375%, learned 4.89375%. Learned palette seeds mix shaded paper colours; this is not merely numerical roundoff or an isolated solver defect.",
      "Printed stripes, dots, lettering and floral ink remain mistaken for cut boundaries. The printed central flower is neither recovered nor shown to be a physically woven motif.",
      "Candy basket and rotated house have unsuitable fixed crops. Palette changes cannot repair their selection. The guitar crop includes background below the lower border. Seven unresolved crops remain unresolved.",
      "Flower, moon, cat, dinosaurs, paired hearts, dragonfly, bird and star retain recognizable motifs, but false thin joins, altered central checks or rounded cell boundaries remain on several.",
      "Nativity, blue/gold figure, and black/red silhouette still lose important details during fitting even when their targets visibly retain them. Pixel agreement alone does not resolve routing.",
      "One stacked-heart target differs by only 37/160000 pixels while fit error changes from 1.0325% to 2.554375%; this separate case has not yet had a deterministic search diagnosis."
    ]
  },
