    "mechanism": "Both arms initialize all 16 count/phase hypotheses. The three-slot shortlist reserves 3x3 for opposing-border evidence. On the learned target, the complexity-based simpler-grid reservation replaces 6x6 with 4x4 phase +1. All three remaining fine grids lose a source region. On RGB, 6x6 survives and colour retention promotes it. Thus the scheduling divergence precedes any timed free-curve refinement.",
    "qualification": "The post-hoc omitted 6x6 grid also passes colour retention on the learned target after the same 150 gradient steps. It is not a validated cutting template and still has 5.59% grid mismatch. No claim that six cuts is the original design; no production count rule has changed."
  },
